# Line endings.
#
# The repository is developed on macOS but is also worked on from Windows 11, where Git
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true. That would check text files out with CRLF, and the POSIX
# shell scripts here are run directly by name — tools/check_no_firmware.sh is a pre-commit
# hook entry — so a CRLF shebang makes the hook fail with "bad interpreter".
#
# Normalise on commit and check out LF everywhere, whatever the local setting is.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Run by sh, so never CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Not firmware, but the same trap: the patches and manifests are byte-compared.
*.json text eol=lf
